1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:05,704
Deep dive: doors and drawers. How the app sizes fronts, why the reveals matter, and how a drawer box is built for Blum TANDEM.

2
00:00:05,704 --> 00:00:19,571
Start with the 24" two-door base, B1. Doors are full overlay: they cover the box edges, with a small gap all round.

3
00:00:19,571 --> 00:00:24,647
Doors: None, One or Pair. A pair on anything over about 21" wide keeps each door light and its swing short.

4
00:00:24,647 --> 00:00:33,571
The Gap is the reveal: 1/8" between the pair and round the edges. Even reveals are what make a kitchen look straight.

5
00:00:33,571 --> 00:00:44,259
So each door is half the width less the gaps, 11-7/8"; and the box height less the toe kick and a gap, 30-7/16".

6
00:00:44,259 --> 00:00:51,383
Every door edge gets 1 mm ABS (L1 L2 W1 W2): doors are handled more than anything else in a kitchen.

7
00:00:51,383 --> 00:01:05,939
Switch to One door and the app asks for the hinge side, the side the door swings from. Pick it to suit the room.

8
00:01:05,939 --> 00:01:12,035
One 24" door is wide and heavy, so back to a pair.

9
00:01:12,035 --> 00:01:27,119
Add one drawer to the same box. Drawers stack from the bottom, so it goes under the doors, and the doors shrink to 24-5/16" to make room.

10
00:01:27,119 --> 00:01:36,220
The drawer front: 6" high, the full width less the gaps, banded on all four edges like a door.

11
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:45,479
The box behind it: two sides, a subfront, a back and a 1/4" HDF bottom. Sides are 18" long for an 18" slide.

12
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:54,747
Box parts are 5/8" (16 mm) board: Blum TANDEM takes sides up to 16 mm. An 18 mm side would not fit the runner.

13
00:01:54,747 --> 00:02:02,599
The box is 5-3/16" high: lower than its front, so the front covers the box and the runners.

14
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:14,953
Not wanted here: back to 0 drawers, and Done. Now the 3-drawer base, B2.

15
00:02:14,953 --> 00:02:24,459
Doors: None, Drawers: 3. Three equal fronts fill the height above the toe kick.

16
00:02:24,459 --> 00:02:30,299
Slide: Auto from depth picks the longest TANDEM that fits, 15, 18 or 21 in. Choose one only for a shallow or odd box.

17
00:02:30,299 --> 00:02:38,357
Box material defaults to the 16 mm drawer board. The 18 mm boards are marked "too thick for TANDEM", so the reason not to use them is right there in the list.

18
00:02:38,357 --> 00:02:48,151
Three drawers, three sets of box parts. The cut list groups them, and the 16 mm parts nest on their own sheet.

19
00:02:48,151 --> 00:03:08,099
Explode to see the three boxes inside, with the runner holes bored in the cabinet sides.

20
00:03:08,099 --> 00:03:13,393
In short: reveals set the door and front sizes, depth sets the slide, and TANDEM sets the box board. The app keeps all three in step.
